# interplay_fifo_pending_full_across: A child's stamp queue holds 128 pending stamps; child 1's opcode 99 faults and 129 NOPs follow, so after 127 of them its thread blocks pushing the 128th: the node's read count already covers that command (Fifo::advance precedes Fifo::push_stamp). Child 2 waits on child 1's last stamp. 0x1028 = 1 publishes stamps up to 128 in one interrupt, the blocked push goes on, stamps 129 and 130 publish one each, and child 2 is released.
